  m_Script: {fileID: 11500000, guid: 0d5562cc34807e2439c5cc188b7351d9, type: 3}
  m_Name: ClientServerSuccessDialog
  m_EditorClassIdentifier: Assembly-CSharp::DialogSequence
  lines:
  - speakerName: Guide
    text: "Both directions answer. The server reached 192.168.1.20 and the client
      reached 192.168.1.10 \u2014 replies from each, no packets lost."
  - speakerName: Guide
    text: That is what makes it a verified link rather than a hopeful one. A ping
      in one direction only proves the request arrived; a reply proves the return
      path works too, and a network that carries traffic one way is not a network.
  - speakerName: Guide
    text: "Horizontal runs terminated, patch panel punched down, both hosts addressed,
      connectivity tested and confirmed. That is the networking job signed off \u2014
      the assessor's sheet asks you to inspect and test what you configured, and
      you just did."
